      "id": "k-green-bean-background-54",
      "topic": "background",
      "summary": "Warm-season annual harvested for immature pods. Frost damages exposed tissues; chilling can slow emergence and vegetative growth. Heat and water stress near flowering can cause poor pod set or blossom loss. Avoid close repetition where bean-specific pathogens occur; rotate according to the identified organism. Fresh-pod production can involve repeated picking; sowing-to-first-pick differs from the full picking period.",
